            <ArticleTitle>Persistent hip pain despite normal radiographs.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>46-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.JAA.0000443971.54105.18</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acetabular fractures are frequently missed on plain view radiographs of the hip and pelvis. A high degree of clinical suspicion for an acetabular fracture should be maintained in any patient with persistent traumatic hip, pelvic, or buttock pain, and inability to ambulate.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
